From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] xmllite: read UTF-16 input longer than two buffers

Purpose: read the user interface files of Windows 7's folder windows,
which are longer than 16 KB.
Windows behavior: IXmlReader reads a UTF-16 stream of any length; Windows
7's DirectUI (explorerframe.dll) passes its UIFILE resources to it as
UTF-16 in memory, with CreateXmlReaderInputWithEncodingName(L"UTF-16").
Wine before: for UTF-16 input, reader_more copied the raw buffer to the
UTF-16 buffer but did not empty it, as it does for other encodings. The
first refill (after the XML declaration) was emptied by the caller; the
second filled the raw buffer, and the third read nothing into the full
buffer and copied the same 8 KB again. Text after it was read twice: an
attribute value came out as "item.lisHost)" and the reader failed in
explorerframe's UIFILE #a000 after "<LineScroller", so the folder window
(Win+E) was destroyed before it showed.
Change: after copying UTF-16 input, the copied bytes are removed from the
raw buffer, keeping an odd last byte for the next read.
Evidence: a probe reading that UIFILE as UTF-16 from a memory stream
failed at 5:545 (0xc00cee3b) and read all 1589 nodes from a file stream;
with this change both read all 1589 nodes. Wine's xmllite reader tests
(2145) pass.
Scope: every program's UTF-16 input to xmllite.
---
 dlls/xmllite/reader.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/xmllite/reader.c b/dlls/xmllite/reader.c
index 27d4fd0..b4acab2 100644
--- a/dlls/xmllite/reader.c
+++ b/dlls/xmllite/reader.c
@@ -1080,9 +1080,17 @@ static HRESULT reader_more(xmlreader *reader)
     /* just copy for UTF-16 case */
     if (cp == 1200)
     {
+        int left;
+
+        len &= ~1;
         readerinput_grow(readerinput, len);
         memcpy(dest->data + dest->written, src->data + src->cur, len);
         dest->written += len;
+        /* get rid of processed data, keeping a partly read character */
+        left = src->written - src->cur - len;
+        memmove(src->data, src->data + src->cur + len, left);
+        src->written = left;
+        src->cur = 0;
     }
     else
     {
